  "attestation": "D-133 closed-loop round 3 fixes on needs-wording (audit of a4bfeed: 2 HIGH, 4 MEDIUM, 1 LOW, one suspected). The impact plan was regenerated (the auditor had blanked its review and test fields). Two deliberate, narrow, fail-safe boundary rules on how answers from Alembic are recorded (both gaps older than D-133). HIGH-1: a digest answer counts as yes (confirm, claim, adopt, apply, keep, revert) only when it is one of the question exact choices; free words are recorded as said (said: prefix, which no reader matches: digest CONFIRMS/CLAIMS/ADOPTS, ms8 apply and revert, verdicts keep, obligations asksChange reads it as a change for the agent; LATER only on an exact Later), and a question of a binding kind (exercise-data-confirm, confirmation-stale, answer-still-correct, fact-disputed, instructor-edit-unasked, unit-unknown-authorship) answered in words is skipped and asked again. Old hand-ins: a record without choices goes through the same rule; corrections and approvals were already exact (round 2). HIGH-2: the record keeps each unit content hash as asked (seen); apply skips an answer whose units changed (the passage changed since it was asked); a record without seen is checked by its one finding basis, else asked again. With it, a passage too long to show keeps its choices again (never pre-chosen) and the question says the page holds the exact text. MEDIUM-3: no sentinel inside scripts; control characters stripped in plainText, lightText, line and block; handinProblems mirrors Alembic oneLine; refs pass a mirror of Alembic normalizePath (coursePath). MEDIUM-4: assistant entry 2,400 bytes, entry evidence bounded, oldest hand-ins dropped above 3 MB, record written compact. MEDIUM-5: a long correction is not pre-chosen and shows the words it removes in full when they fit. MEDIUM-7: off-page texts budgeted first; a suggestion that cannot be shown drops Apply and says it cannot be applied from Alembic (probe adapted to accept that alternative). LOW-6: orz-markdown exported per-document budgets mirrored with its chemLength. Suspected (ms8-verdicts suggestion path): the unasked-edit question now names every holder of the registered text the edited unit holds (as adoptInstructorText adopts them); unchanged ids when the unit holds no registered text; new test in redteam-r4-confidence fails without the fix. Probes adopted as tests/needs-wording.audit3.test.mjs (HIGH-1 adapted: HIGH-2 restores choices, so it answers a choice-less record with a matching seen, and adds a non-binding kind) and registered for req.host.alembic-needs-wording and req.host.alembic-needs-apply; a HIGH-2 main-path test added to alembic-needs-wording. CHANGELOG Unreleased records both rules plainly; VERSION unchanged. Reviewed every required item. Tests: the 36 required plus alembic-needs, alembic-needs-wording, needs-wording.audit 1-3, job-release, and redteam-r4, r5, r6, r7 (logged, order), d49-decisions and verdict-path for the ms8 change: 669 passed, 0 failed (COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed, concurrency 2, one test process under the shared lock).",
